      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T06:27:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Greg. I like keeping MakeGLBackendTexture literal, but moving the logic into\nGetGLBackendFormat can\u0027t be a single-file change -- it needs a new parameter and every\nfunction that calls it has to be updated to pass that parameter. The reason:\n\nThe downgrade must rely on isRenderable: only sampled-only buffers can become\nGL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES, render targets must stay a renderable 2D format, or they fail\nisFormatRenderable() and SkSurface creation breaks. The current GetGLBackendFormat api only gets (dContext, bufferFormat, requireKnownFormat), and bufferFormat alone can\u0027t tell \"sampled\" from \"render target\" -- that lives one level up in the AHB usage bits. So isRenderable has to be threaded in.\n\nTo move it into GetGLBackendFormat, these are the changes we\u0027d need:\n1. include/android/GrAHardwareBufferUtils.h\n   - Add `bool isRenderable` to GetGLBackendFormat() and to GetBackendFormat().\n2. src/gpu/ganesh/gl/AHardwareBufferGL.cpp\n   - GetGLBackendFormat(): take isRenderable, do the read-only to external decision here.\n   - MakeGLBackendTexture(): drop the inline decision, import backendFormat as-is.\n3. src/gpu/ganesh/GrAHardwareBufferUtils.cpp\n   - GetBackendFormat(): forward isRenderable to GetGLBackendFormat (Vulkan unchanged).\n4. Call sites:\n   - SkSurface_AndroidFactories.cpp: isRenderable \u003d true.\n   - SkImage_GaneshFactories_Android.cpp: compute from AHARDWAREBUFFER_USAGE_GPU_FRAMEBUFFER.\n   - GrAHardwareBufferImageGenerator.cpp/MultiPictureDocumentTest.cpp: false (defaulted arg).\n\nIf you\u0027re OK with above API change I\u0027ll push it. Otherwise I can keep the decision\nin MakeGLBackendTexture, where isRenderable is already available.\nWhichever you prefer, thanks!",
